NASA HERA Requirements Moonscape and Robots Planning Phase v1.01

Executive Summary
The NASA HERA Moonscape and Robots project is designed to improve the realism and engagement of the Human Exploration Research Analog (HERA) program by adding a remotely operated robotic lunar exploration component. This project will develop an 8 ft × 8 ft portable lunar landscape model or a VR model, along with robotic systems that HERA participants, known as HERAnauts, can operate during their 45-day isolation missions.

This effort supports the NASA HUNCH program by integrating educational development, engineering, and mission realism. The goal is to create a realistic lunar exploration environment that allows participants to experience mission tasks similar to those encountered by astronauts while maintaining the operational discipline and communication delays associated with a simulated space mission.

