Planning Stage
The planning stage is crucial because it establishes the requirements for both the lunar landscape and the robotic systems. The lunar landscape section defines the exact dimensions, construction requirements, portability needs, and visual barriers required to maintain mission immersion. The robotic system section outlines the need for four specialized robots with specific capabilities in transportation and manipulation, all controlled via Bluetooth within a 100-meter range.

This phase ensures that all technical specifications, including camera systems, power requirements, materials, and control interfaces, are clearly defined before implementation begins.

Project Overview
The project overview section establishes the basic framework for the entire initiative. Its purpose is to enhance HERA missions by giving participants realistic lunar exploration activities that maintain psychological immersion in the space environment.

The scope goes beyond the physical construction of the moonscape and robots. It also includes the control systems, protocols, integration requirements, testing procedures, and operational scenarios necessary for successful implementation.

